Subject: Justification for the Cantor M2B Windows Sys Compile Probe Lock Revision

& [Claim] is narrow
  + [statement] replace the impossible byte-identical lock invariant with one exact local dependency-edge delta and retain every no-call and no-effect gate
  + [confidence] is high

& [Support] is concrete
  + [locked_failure] Cargo refused the 0.1 direct dependency under --locked before compilation
  + [Cargo_model] an isolated offline worktree produced exactly one added lock line and no package-universe change
  + [pre_lock_sha256] is 7b2e1e879e387ccff1cf1e04de4ace1d72eb006d1443192ab26629f0c3a884a5
  + [modeled_post_lock_sha256] is ff20148aa6ff3c2774d07d454bc900f4f81d5594bd8f8e49af2a43217b7ee73a
  + [package_count] remains 112
  + [package_identity] windows-sys remains 0.61.2 with its existing checksum

& [WhyNotPreserveByteIdentity] is causal
  + [reason] Cargo.lock records local package dependency edges
  + [consequence] a new direct edge must alter the cantor_ecosystem package entry
  + [alternative] avoiding the lock delta would require avoiding the direct dependency, contradicting the ABI-probe purpose

& [WhyExactSemanticDelta] is security preserving
  + [reason] accepting an unconstrained lock update could hide upgrades or unrelated dependency drift
  + [gate] exact one-line diff plus exact post-hash plus unchanged package universe
  + [result] only the intended relationship changes

& [Counterarguments] are answered
  + [counterargument] use transitive windows-sys without a direct dependency
  + [answer] that makes the consumer relationship implicit and does not provide a stable manifest contract
  + [counterargument] permit any Cargo-generated lockfile
  + [answer] Cargo output is still subject to repository policy and must match the isolated model exactly
  + [counterargument] proceed directly to Windows calls
  + [answer] declaration availability and runtime effect authority are separate risk boundaries

& [Invalidation] is explicit
  + [condition] any package addition, removal, version, source, checksum, nonlocal edge, feature, call, unsafe, production, physical effect, stale evidence, or overclaim drift
  + [response] stop, remove unproven implementation, record the fault, and reprocess source before continuation

& [Rollback] is bounded
  + [Cargo] remove the exact target dependency
  + [lock] remove only the exact local windows-sys edge and restore the pre-hash
  + [test] remove the Windows-only integration probe
  + [production] no rollback because production Rust must not change
